WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.840
A credit score is one part of

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:04.480
a mortgage decision. It doesn't explain every

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.180
question about your situation.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:08.420
Start with the report behind it.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.880
Look for information you don't recognize or

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.360
believe is wrong. Checking your own credit

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.380
report doesn't hurt your scores.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.880
A lender's credit inquiry is a separate

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.360
kind of request. Before making a change

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.400
because of something you heard, ask what

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.980
it means for your particular situation.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.120
The credit worksheet helps you describe that

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.940
question. Keep account numbers out.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.480
Review before sending your answers to me,

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.410
or print the page for yourself.
